# EMDR — git commit & push

## When finishing a coding turn (default — no ask needed)

If this turn **changed product/code/docs/rules** (not pure Q&A / plan-only):

1. Hard gate (required): `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `ReadLints` on touched files. Fix failures before committing.
2. **Always commit** relevant files in the **same turn** — do not wait for the user to ask.
3. Do **not** auto-push on finish. Push only when the user asked (see below), unless they already said ship/push this turn.
4. Skip auto-commit only when there is nothing to commit (no product diffs) or only noise (`.next`, scratch).

Commit message: concise why-focused; include any rule/docs tweak from the same turn.

## When the user asks to commit / push / ship

If they say **commit**, **push**, **commit push**, **ship**, or similar (any language):

1. Same hard gate as above.
2. Commit all relevant product/code/docs/rules changes.
3. **Push** to the tracked remote in the same turn, unless they explicitly said **commit only** / **bez push** / **samo commit**.
4. Do not wait for a second confirmation.
5. If they say commit after a coding session (even without “push”), treat as **commit + push** — that remains the default when they *ask*.

## Reminders (push lag)

At the end of a turn, if there are **local commits ahead of origin** or a large unpushed history, and they did not just push, one short reminder is OK: e.g. “Lokalni commitovi nisu na origin — hoćeš push?”

Skip if they just pushed or only noise remains.

## What not to commit

- `.env`, credentials, `node_modules`, `.next`, scratch `scripts/_tmp-*`, `*.tsbuildinfo`
- Unrelated untracked assets unless part of the task
- Do not update git config; do not `--force` to `main`/`master`

## Gates note

Do **not** run full `npm run build` as a local pre-commit gate (Actions Docker covers compile). Lint + tests are enough.
